From: LocalAI
Subject: [PATCH] capi: hoist OrEmpty out of the extern "C" block

src/capi/vllm_c.cpp wraps the whole ABI surface in one `extern "C" {`, so
file-local helpers declared inside it inherit C linkage even when they sit
in an anonymous namespace. The video slice (ABI v12) added one that returns
std::string, which Apple Clang reports as -Wreturn-type-c-linkage; vllm.cpp
promotes it with a target-wide -Werror and the metal-darwin-arm64 build of
this backend fails to compile.

It cannot be waved off from outside the engine: vllm_cpp_set_warnings adds
`-Wall -Wextra -Werror` as PRIVATE target options, which land after anything
a consumer puts in CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, and -Wall re-enables the -Wreturn-type
group that -Wreturn-type-c-linkage belongs to. Position is the only fix.

Moving the definition above the `extern "C" {` gives it C++ linkage. It is
file-local and never called across the boundary, so nothing else changes.

Carried here rather than in the engine because the pin is a released SHA.
DROP THIS FILE when VLLM_CPP_VERSION moves to a commit that carries the fix
upstream; the Makefile's `git apply` then fails loudly rather than silently
skipping it.

diff --git a/src/capi/vllm_c.cpp b/src/capi/vllm_c.cpp
--- a/src/capi/vllm_c.cpp
+++ b/src/capi/vllm_c.cpp
@@ -460,6 +460,15 @@
   request->done.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
 }
 
+// Used by the video entry points below. It lives OUT here, above the `extern
+// "C"` block, because everything inside that block inherits C linkage - even a
+// file-local helper in an anonymous namespace - and Apple Clang rejects a
+// C-linkage function returning std::string under -Wreturn-type-c-linkage. The
+// target-wide `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` lands after any -Wno- a consumer can pass
+// on CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS and re-enables the group, so it cannot be waved off from
+// the outside. Position is the fix.
+std::string OrEmpty(const char* s) { return s == nullptr ? std::string() : std::string(s); }
+
 }  // namespace
 
 extern "C" {
@@ -1396,12 +1405,6 @@
   return p;
 }
 
-namespace {
-
-std::string OrEmpty(const char* s) { return s == nullptr ? std::string() : std::string(s); }
-
-}  // namespace
-
 // The opaque video handle: owns the loaded checkpoint set + staged weights.
 struct vllm_video_engine {
   std::unique_ptr<vllm::multimodal::MiniMaxH3VideoEngine> engine;
